# Server-side filters

- Filters live in URL search params (`validateSearch` + `replace: true`) and are sent to tRPC. Empty strings are omitted from the URL. Text search (`q`) is local while typing and written after ~300ms debounce.
- Matching is SQL (`projects.list`, `audit.list`) or a server procedure (`dashboard.metrics`, `invoices.list`). Never `array.filter` on a fetched collection to decide what is visible.
- Out of scope: DataTable sort/pagination on an already-filtered page result may stay in memory. Audit is the exception — it already keyset-paginates and sorts on the server.
- Loading uses `FilterPending` around the results (filters stay interactive): skeleton on first load, muted results plus a bordô scan on refetch. Do not blank the page with “Carregando…”.
- Dropdown option lists come from an unfiltered options payload so a selected filter cannot hide its own controls.
- After mutations, invalidate `["projects"]`, `["dashboard"]`, `["invoices"]`, and `["audit"]`.
- Kanban drag-end calls `move` for the dragged card only. Never `replaceProjects` with a filtered subset.
